    "final_answer": "I have gathered all the information I need from the article. Let me now provide my final answer.\n\n## Task Completed Successfully\n\nI used Google Search to find an article about the major differences between American English and British English.\n\n### Article Found:\n**\"British English vs. American English: Discover Key Differences\"**\n- **Source:** Bay Atlantic University (BAU) Blog\n- **URL:** https://bau.edu/blog/british-english-vs-american-english/\n- **Published:** November 13, 2024\n- **Author:** Bay Atlantic University\n\n### Major Differences Explained in the Article:\n\nThe article states: *\"The biggest differences between British and American English are in spelling, grammar, and pronunciation.\"*\n\n#### 1. **Spelling Differences**\n- **\"-our\" (British) vs. \"-or\" (American):**\n  - Colour vs. Color\n  - Favour vs. Favor\n  - Labour vs. Labor\n- **\"-re\" (British) vs. \"-er\" (American):**\n  - Centre vs. Center\n  - Metre vs. Meter\n  - Theatre vs. Theater\n- **\"-ise\" (British) vs. \"-ize\" (American):**\n  - Realise vs. Realize\n  - Organise vs. Organize\n  - Apologise vs. Apologize\n- **Doubling of consonants & \"-ce/-se\" endings:**\n  - Travelling vs. Traveling\n  - Defence vs. Defense\n\n#### 2. **Grammar and Punctuation Differences**\n- Verb tenses and forms\n- Use of prepositions\n- Collective nouns (e.g., \"team is\" vs. \"team are\")\n- Punctuation conventions (e.g., placement of periods/commas relative to quotation marks)\n- Tense usage differences:\n  - British: *\"I've just eaten\"*\n  - American: *\"I just ate\"* (preferring simple past over present perfect)\n\n#### 3. **Pronunciation Variations**\n- Different vowel sounds and stress patterns between the two variants (e.g., the pronunciation of words like \"schedule,\" \"advertisement,\" and \"aluminum/aluminium\").\n\nThe article emphasizes that these differences matter for **academic and business communication**, where consistent spelling and grammar are essential for clarity and professionalism across English-speaking regions.\n\nOther relevant results from the search included:\n- British Council's \"LearnEnglish\" article\n- Wikipedia's \"Comparison of American and British English\"\n- British Council Indonesia Foundation's article on the differences",
